province = 74
blurb = "Depicts a rainy afternoon at the Kiyomizu Kiyomizu-dō temple in Ueno Park, Tōkyō.

The temple was built in 1631, modeled after Kyōto's famous Kiyomizu-dera. It features a raised, pillared veranda overlooking Shinobazu Pond and is celebrated for its Moon Pine tree, depicted in numerous ukiyo-e prints. You can visit the temple and see the (current generation of the) tree even today."
